      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "The flaw drops function-valued TLS options such as checkServerIdentity. node-gyp's only undici use is lib/download.js, which fetches with an Agent or EnvHttpProxyAgent wrapped in RetryAgent and passes only string ca options (connect, requestTls, proxyTls = { ca }); it passes no function-valued TLS option, so nothing is dropped."
